cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "pde-operator-experiment: a classical solver, a PINN, a DeepONet and an FNO on one elliptic PDE with an exact solution"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/pde-operator-experiment"
url: "https://diogoribeiro7.github.io/pde-operator-experiment/"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible comparison of a finite-difference solver, a physics-informed
  neural network, a DeepONet and a Fourier neural operator on the
  one-dimensional elliptic equation -(a u')' = 1 with random coefficients,
  scored against an exact solution. It measures in-distribution accuracy,
  training-set size, distribution shift, resolution transfer and cost, with
  the classical solver treated as a competitor on equal terms.
keywords:
  - scientific machine learning
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - neural operators
  - DeepONet
  - Fourier neural operator
  - finite differences
  - reproducibility
